# Overloaded Damn destroys each creature at once (CR 702.96a, 701.8), skipping any that are indestructible. On turn three
# Bot1 overloads it with a Sol Ring and two Plains, with its own Ornithopter in play beside Bot2's two. Bot2 answers by
# giving one of its Ornithopters indestructible with Revitalizing Repast: that one lives, and the other two die. Damn
# never targets, so the shielded creature's being a legal target in response is irrelevant here.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
Damn
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Revitalizing Repast
Swamp x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Damn.Cast(Ability: Overload)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Revitalizing Repast.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Damn; Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Revitalizing Repast
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
